From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 11:05:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mfmediaengine: Read media type stream attributes

IMFMediaEngineEx::GetStreamAttribute() is also used for media type
attributes. AVPro enumerates streams with MF_MT_MAJOR_TYPE and then reads
MF_MT_FRAME_RATE from the discovered video stream. Those attributes are on
the stream's current media type rather than its stream descriptor, causing
both major-type queries to fail and leaving AVPro with an invalid stream
index and a reported frame rate of zero.

Keep stream descriptor attributes authoritative, but fall back to the
current media type when an attribute is not present there.

diff --git a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
--- a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
@@ -3778,6 +3778,21 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI media_engine_GetStreamAttribute(IMFMediaEngineEx *iface, D
                 stream_index, &selected, &sd)))
         {
             hr = IMFStreamDescriptor_GetItem(sd, attribute, value);
+            if (hr == MF_E_ATTRIBUTENOTFOUND)
+            {
+                IMFMediaTypeHandler *handler;
+                IMFMediaType *media_type;
+
+                if (SUCCEEDED(hr = IMFStreamDescriptor_GetMediaTypeHandler(sd, &handler)))
+                {
+                    if (SUCCEEDED(hr = IMFMediaTypeHandler_GetCurrentMediaType(handler, &media_type)))
+                    {
+                        hr = IMFMediaType_GetItem(media_type, attribute, value);
+                        IMFMediaType_Release(media_type);
+                    }
+                    IMFMediaTypeHandler_Release(handler);
+                }
+            }
             IMFStreamDescriptor_Release(sd);
         }
     }
